MUMPS 5.8.2: avoid redundant atomic writes to pivot extrema (hsolve P13).

The L0 subtree workers share DKEEP(19:21): minimum pivot, minimum non-null
pivot, maximum pivot. All callers supply absolute pivot values. These extrema
move monotonically during factorization. Read each statistic atomically first;
when the pivot cannot change it, skip the original atomic min/max update.
A concurrent writer can only strengthen the bound. Writers still use atomic
min/max (never a plain assignment), so races cannot lose an extreme value.
Negated comparisons keep unordered values on the original update path.
The serial path, pivot selection, null detection and arithmetic are unchanged.
Applies to all four arithmetics; no new KEEP entries or application settings.

Apply after mumps-5.8.2-l0-blocking.patch with tools/dev/build_mumps.sh --patch.
Validation and timings: results/p13_measurements.md and p13_extrema_probe.cpp.
This is an hsolve modification of MUMPS, distributed under CeCILL-C.

--- a/src/sfac_front_aux.F
+++ b/src/sfac_front_aux.F
@@ -2538,6 +2538,7 @@
       REAL, INTENT(INOUT) :: DKEEP(230)
       LOGICAL, INTENT(IN) :: NULLPIVOT
       INTEGER, INTENT(IN) :: KEEP(500)
+      REAL :: CURRENT
       IF (KEEP(405).EQ.0) THEN
         DKEEP(21) = max(DKEEP(21), DIAG)
         DKEEP(19) = min(DKEEP(19), DIAG)
@@ -2545,16 +2546,35 @@
           DKEEP(20) = min(DKEEP(20), DIAG)
         ENDIF
       ELSE
-!$OMP   ATOMIC UPDATE
-        DKEEP(21) = max(DKEEP(21), DIAG)
+C       Extrema only move outwards during factorization. An atomic read
+C       can skip an update that cannot change them; a concurrent update
+C       only makes that skip safer. Keep the atomic min/max for writers.
+C       Negated comparisons retain the update path for unordered values.
+!$OMP   ATOMIC READ
+        CURRENT = DKEEP(21)
 !$OMP   END ATOMIC
-!$OMP   ATOMIC UPDATE
-        DKEEP(19) = min(DKEEP(19), DIAG)
+        IF (.NOT.(DIAG.LE.CURRENT)) THEN
+!$OMP     ATOMIC UPDATE
+          DKEEP(21) = max(DKEEP(21), DIAG)
+!$OMP     END ATOMIC
+        ENDIF
+!$OMP   ATOMIC READ
+        CURRENT = DKEEP(19)
 !$OMP   END ATOMIC
+        IF (.NOT.(DIAG.GE.CURRENT)) THEN
+!$OMP     ATOMIC UPDATE
+          DKEEP(19) = min(DKEEP(19), DIAG)
+!$OMP     END ATOMIC
+        ENDIF
         IF (.NOT.NULLPIVOT) THEN
-!$OMP     ATOMIC UPDATE
-          DKEEP(20) = min(DKEEP(20), DIAG)
+!$OMP     ATOMIC READ
+          CURRENT = DKEEP(20)
 !$OMP     END ATOMIC
+          IF (.NOT.(DIAG.GE.CURRENT)) THEN
+!$OMP       ATOMIC UPDATE
+            DKEEP(20) = min(DKEEP(20), DIAG)
+!$OMP       END ATOMIC
+          ENDIF
         ENDIF
       ENDIF
       RETURN
